# --- from dark-gray/kitty.conf ---
# dark-gray - kitty OVERRIDES.
#
# Normally leave this empty, as it is now. apply.sh GENERATES
# ~/.config/kitty/current-theme.conf from the term_* names in palette.css, so
# the terminal palette lives in the same file as everything else. Whatever is
# in here is appended AFTER the generated block, so it wins.
#
# This file used to be the whole kitty integration, and it was empty, which is
# why kitty was never themed at all: apply.sh's `-s` guard skipped it and
# current-theme.conf still held "Adapta Nokto Maia" with a #222D31 background.
# It cannot fail that way any more - an empty file now means "no overrides"
# rather than "no theme".
#
# Only put things here that palette.css genuinely cannot express, e.g.
#
#   background_opacity 0.9
#   background_image ~/Pictures/term-bg.png
#
# Colour values belong in palette.css. Note that non-colour settings do not
# work with `kitty @ set-colors`, so they need a kitty restart regardless.
